## TypeScript End-User API for 3D Camera Animation (Prioritizing Helpfulness & Verbosity)

This API aims to be intuitive,  flexible, and robust for controlling 3D camera animations in TypeScript, striking a balance between ease of use and comprehensive functionality.

**Core Concepts & Structure:**

1. **`CameraController` Class:**  The central hub managing all animation aspects. Instances represent individual cameras.

   ```typescript
   class CameraController {
       constructor(scene: THREE.Scene, initialCamera: THREE.PerspectiveCamera); // Scene & starting camera required

       // Animation Definition & Playback
       animate(animation: AnimationSpec): Promise<void>; 
       play(animationName: string): Promise<void>; // Play by named animation
       stop(): void;
       pauseResume(): void; // Toggle playback state

       // Camera Properties (Direct Manipulation)
       position: THREE.Vector3;
       target: THREE.Object3D; // Target to track
       fov: number;
       near: number;
       far: number;
       updateProjectionMatrix(): void; // Manual matrix update if needed

       // Animation Specification (AnimationSpec) Type
       static defineAnimation(name: string, keyframes: Keyframe[]): AnimationSpec; 
   }
   ```

2. **`Keyframe` Structure:**  Building blocks of animations, defining camera states at specific times.

   ```typescript
   interface Keyframe {
       time: number; // Seconds into animation duration
       position: THREE.Vector3;
       target: THREE.Object3D | null; // Optional target object
       fov: number;
       otherProps: { [key: string]: any }; //  Extras (e.g., rotation, easing)
   }
   ```

3. **`AnimationSpec` Object:**  Holds a named animation and its `keyframes`.

   ```typescript
   type AnimationSpec = {
       name: string;
       keyframes: Keyframe[];
       duration: number; // Total animation length in seconds
       easing: EasingFunction; //  Optional easing function (linear, easeInOut, etc.)
       loop: boolean; // Loop playback
   };
   ```

