##  TypeScript API for 3D Camera Animation (Prioritizing Helpfulness & Verbosity)

This API aims to provide a flexible and intuitive way for end-users (developers integrating 3D visuals) to control camera animations in TypeScript, balancing ease of use with comprehensive functionality.

**Core Concepts & Structure:**

1. **`CameraController` Class:**  The central hub managing all animation aspects. Instances represent individual cameras.

   ```typescript
   class CameraController {
       constructor(scene: THREE.Scene, initialPosition: THREE.Vector3, target?: THREE.Object3D); // Scene & starting pose

       // Animation Definition & Playback
       addAnimation(name: string, animationData: AnimationData): this;  
       play(animationName: string, options?: PlaybackOptions): void;
       stop(animationName?: string): void;
       pause(animationName?: string): void;
       resume(animationName?: string): void;

       // Manual Control (Interleaved with Animations)
       setPosition(position: THREE.Vector3): this;
       lookAt(target: THREE.Object3D): this;
       setFov(fov: number): this;
       update(): void; // Syncs camera state with scene (essential for real-time)

       // Animation Data Structure (defined separately)
       static AnimationData = {
           keyframes: Array<{ time: number, position: THREE.Vector3, rotation: THREE.Euler, fov: number }>,
           duration: number, // in seconds
           easing: 'linear' | 'easeInQuad' | 'easeOutQuad' | ... (common easing functions)
       };

       // Playback Options for fine-grained control
       static PlaybackOptions = {
           loop: boolean,
           speed: number,  // Playback rate multiplier
           startTime: number // Start at a specific time within the animation
       };
   }
   ```

2. **Animation Data (`AnimationData`):**  Structured keyframes define camera movements over time.

